        "original_id": "72eee2c4-e5aa-5291-8c62-768f0e9f37a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carl Barât, Jesse Michaels\n- Bands: The Libertines, Dirty Pretty Things, The Jackals, Operation Ivy, Big Rig\n- Places: Berkeley, California, San Francisco Bay Area\n- Products: Expansive Heart, Carl Barât's solo album\n- Companies: Lookout!\n\nFacts:\n- Carl Barât was born on 6 June 1978 and is a British musician.\n- Carl Barât is best known as the co-frontman of The Libertines with Peter Doherty.\n- Carl Barât was the frontman and lead guitarist of Dirty Pretty Things.\n- Carl Barât debuted a solo album in 2010.\n- Carl Barât announced the creation of The Jackals in 2014.\n- Jesse Michaels is a songwriter, vocalist, guitarist, and artist from Berkeley, California.\n- Jesse Michaels is best known as the vocalist for Operation Ivy.\n- Big Rig was a punk band from the San Francisco Bay Area fronted by Jesse Michaels.\n- Expansive Heart was the only release by Big Rig.\n- Lookout! released Expansive Heart.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a69cb792-b49a-5a14-9044-501643ad0e6e",
        "text": "Page: Carl Barât. Sentence: Carlos Ashley Raphael Barât (born 6 June 1978) is a British musician, best known for being the co-frontman with Peter Doherty of the garage rock band The Libertines.\nPage: Carl Barât. Sentence: He was the frontman and lead guitarist of Dirty Pretty Things, and in 2010 debuted a solo album.\nPage: Carl Barât. Sentence: In 2014 he announced the creation of his new band, The Jackals.\nPage: Jesse Michaels. Sentence: Jesse Michaels is a songwriter, vocalist, guitarist and artist from Berkeley, California.\nPage: Jesse Michaels. Sentence: He is most well known as the vocalist for the ska punk band Operation Ivy.\nPage: Big Rig (band). Sentence: Big Rig was a punk band from the San Francisco Bay Area fronted by singer/songwriter Jesse Michaels.\nPage: Expansive Heart. Sentence: Expansive Heart is the only piece ever released by punk band Big Rig, it was released on the Lookout!",
